# Frontend Standards

- Use React + TypeScript components focused on rendering API state.
- Do not hardcode events, endings, scoring, unlock rules, or attribute effects in the UI.
- Fetch game state and ranking from the backend API contracts documented in `docs/api.md`.
- Keep screens under `frontend/src/pages`, reusable UI under `frontend/src/components`, and API calls under `frontend/src/api`.
- Components should accept explicit props and avoid hidden global state for game progression.
- The frontend may cache the last player id for convenience, but SQLite-backed API state is the source of truth.
- Keep the layout responsive for desktop and mobile from the first implementation.
- When changing flows visible to the player, update `docs/architecture.md` or `docs/game-rules.md` if behavior changes.
